# Phase 5, step 6: PX4 on U54 hart 1 (flight control) and Linux SMP on U54 harts 2-4 (mission
# computer), RPMsg between them as in Phase 4 (sim/phase4/rpmsg.resc), with px4.elf in place of the
# NSH image. Virtqueues in shared DDR, notifications through the Mi-V IHC (sim/peripherals/MiV_IHC.cs).
# Linux reaches the IHC through the Microchip SBI extension in our OpenSBI (sw/br2-chipwings/patches/opensbi).
# The E51 is held halted (HSS's job on the board).
#
#   0x80000000  OpenSBI fw_jump (generic platform), harts 2-4
#   0x80200000  Linux Image with the Buildroot rootfs as initramfs
#   0x8A000000  Linux device tree; a1 points harts 2-4 at it
#   0xA2300000  RPMsg resource table (NuttX g_shmem in px4.elf)
#   0xA2400000  vrings + RPMsg buffers
#   0xA2450000  PX4 (boards/chipwings/mpfs-hart1), hart 1; code at 0xA2450000, RAM at 0xA3050000;
#               all of 0xA2000000-0xA403FFFF is reserved no-map in the Linux device tree
#   0x50000000  Mi-V IHC; hart 1 -> PLIC 180, hart 2 -> PLIC 179
#
# Build:  sw/build-px4.sh && sw/build-linux.sh
# Run:    sim/phase5/run.sh [gui|headless] linux     (the script does not call `start`; run.sh does)
# Consoles (also logged to logs/):
#   PX4 NSH    MMUART1 -> telnet localhost $nshport   (default 33457)
#   Linux      MMUART3 -> telnet localhost $linuxport (default 33458), root/root

$px4?=$ORIGIN/../../sw/out/px4/chipwings_mpfs-hart1_default.elf
$images?=$ORIGIN/../../sw/br2-out/images
$opensbi?=$images/fw_jump.elf
$kernel?=$images/Image
$dtb?=$images/chipwings-mpfs-linux.dtb
$nshport?=33457
$linuxport?=33458
$nshlog?=$ORIGIN/logs/px4-mmuart1.log
$linuxlog?=$ORIGIN/logs/linux-mmuart3.log

# Our platform = stock polarfire-soc.repl + interrupt-safe harts and CLINT + Mi-V IHC (sim/platforms/chipwings-mpfs.repl)
include $ORIGIN/../peripherals/SafeIrqRiscV64.cs
include $ORIGIN/../peripherals/SafeIpiCoreLevelInterruptor.cs
include $ORIGIN/../peripherals/MiV_IHC.cs

using sysbus
mach create "uav"
machine LoadPlatformDescription $ORIGIN/../platforms/chipwings-mpfs.repl

# Errors only; the PolarFire model is very chatty at WARNING level.
logLevel 3

# Harts see each other's (and the peripherals') events only at time-quantum boundaries. At the default
# 100 us, PX4's HRT callouts ran up to 100 us late whenever Linux idled (measured: 22% in the 51-100 us
# bucket of perf latency, none with PX4 alone; at 10 us nothing was later than 20 us). Hardware has no such
# floor. 10 us keeps the control loops' timing close to real; the idle real-time ratio stays ~1.
emulation SetGlobalQuantum "0.00001"


e51 IsHalted true

macro reset
"""
    sysbus LoadELF $px4 false u54_1
    sysbus LoadELF $opensbi false u54_2
    sysbus LoadBinary $kernel 0x80200000
    sysbus LoadBinary $dtb 0x8a000000
    u54_3 PC 0x80000000
    u54_4 PC 0x80000000
    u54_2 SetRegisterUlong 11 0x8a000000
    u54_3 SetRegisterUlong 11 0x8a000000
    u54_4 SetRegisterUlong 11 0x8a000000
"""
runMacro $reset

mmuart1 CreateFileBackend $nshlog true
emulation CreateServerSocketTerminal $nshport "nsh" false
connector Connect mmuart1 nsh

mmuart3 CreateFileBackend $linuxlog true
emulation CreateServerSocketTerminal $linuxport "linux" false
connector Connect mmuart3 linux
